; Import library definition for Rust std's `-lsynchronization` on mingw targets.
;
; Rust's std links `synchronization` for its WaitOnAddress-based thread parking
; (library/std/src/sys/sync/futex/windows.rs). Upstream rust-mingw ships
; `libsynchronization.a`, but rust-overlay's toolchain does not include that
; self-contained component, and Zig's bundled mingw-w64 only carries the
; `api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0` apiset definition — so every link fails with:
;
;   error: unable to find dynamic system library "synchronization" using
;          strategy paths_first. searched paths: none
;
; WaitOnAddress/WakeByAddress{Single,All} are exported by
; api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll (Windows 8+, resolved through the API set
; schema), so generating the missing import library from that apiset is
; equivalent to the upstream one. xzar.sh turns this file into
; `libsynchronization.a` with `zig dlltool` before cross-building for Windows.
LIBRARY api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll
EXPORTS
WaitOnAddress
WakeByAddressAll
WakeByAddressSingle
